---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Flow Resources — Howie Seay"
  description="A curated guide to flow cytometry: communities, ebooks, tutorials, panel design, spectral resources, training, and jobs."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Flow Resources</p>
      <h1>Flow chose you</h1>
      <p>
        The communities worth joining, the books worth reading, the software worth learning, and the
        courses worth the time &mdash; everything I wish someone had handed me on day one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="section tight">
    <div class="container">

      <h2 class="res-head">Online Communities (A to Z)</h2>
        <div class="table-wrapper">
          <table class="alt">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Name</th>
                <th>Description</th>
                <th>Year Est.</th>
                <th>Rating</th>
                <th>Link</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Chromocyte</td>
                <td>A flow cytometry experimental design website.</td>
                <td>2009</td>
                <td>3/5</td>
                <td><a href="https://www.chromocyte.com/" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>ISAC-net</td>
                <td>Born from ISAC.</td>
                <td>Rebooted in 2018</td>
                <td>3/5</td>
                <td><a href="https://isac-net.org/login.aspx" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Purdue Cytometry List</td>
                <td>This list is for the discussion of cytometry. Both image and flow cytometry topics are welcomed. Easily the best resource for flow cytometry information.</td>
                <td>1992</td>
                <td>5/5</td>
                <td><a href="http://www.cyto.purdue.edu/" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>r/cytometry</td>
                <td>A Reddit community dedicated to flow cytometry, cell sorting, and CyTOF.</td>
                <td>2017</td>
                <td>3/5</td>
                <td><a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/cytometry/" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Scientific Community Imaging Forum</td>
                <td>A discussion forum for scientific image software sponsored by COBA. A good resource for imaging cytometry.</td>
                <td>TBD</td>
                <td>5/5</td>
                <td><a href="https://forum.image.sc/" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2 class="res-head">Flow Cytometry eBooks</h2>
        <div class="table-wrapper">
          <table class="alt">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Book Title</th>
                <th>Edition</th>
                <th>Author</th>
                <th>Year</th>
                <th>Description</th>
                <th>eBook Link</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Evaluation of Voltration Approaches for Optimal Data Acquisition in Flow Cytometry</td>
                <td>Thesis</td>
                <td>Meredith Weglarz</td>
                <td>2018</td>
                <td>A great summarization of different techniques for maximizing flow cytometer sensitivity</td>
                <td><a href="https://dash.harvard.edu/bitstream/handle/1/37945126/WEGLARZ-DOCUMENT-2018.pdf" target="_blank" class="button fit small">View</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><em>Flow Cytometry - A Basic Introduction</em></td>
                <td>Web</td>
                <td>Michael G. Ormerod</td>
                <td>2008</td>
                <td>Concise and thorough.</td>
                <td><a href="https://www.beckman.com/resources/reading-material/ebooks/first-principles/view" target="_blank" class="button fit small">View</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><em>Flow Cytometry: First Principles</em></td>
                <td>2nd</td>
                <td>Alice Longobardi</td>
                <td>2001</td>
                <td>A bit dated, but still a nice read to flip through</td>
                <td><a href="https://www.beckman.com/resources/reading-material/ebooks/first-principles/view" target="_blank" class="button fit small">View</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><em>How to Become a Flow Cytometry Expert in 4 Days</em></td>
                <td>1st</td>
                <td>Marketing Department</td>
                <td>n/a</td>
                <td>A decent "handbook" for learning Flow Cytometry.</td>
                <td><a href="https://www.bosterbio.com/media/pdf/Flow_Cytometry_FACS_Troubleshooting_Handbook.pdf" target="_blank" class="button fit small">View</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><em>Imaging Flow Cytometry: Methods and Protocols</em></td>
                <td>1st</td>
                <td>Natasha S. Barteneva &amp; Ivan A. Vorobjev</td>
                <td>2016</td>
                <td>Principles of Amnis Imaging Flow Cytometry on p. 13</td>
                <td><a href="https://www.amrepflow.org.au/public/documents/ImagingFlowCytometryMethodsBook.pdf" target="_blank" class="button fit small">View</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><em>Practical Flow Cytometry</em></td>
                <td>4th</td>
                <td>Howard M. Shapiro</td>
                <td>2003</td>
                <td>No question &mdash; the Flow Cytometry Bible</td>
                <td><a href="https://www.beckman.com/resources/reading-material/ebooks/practical-flow-cytometry/view" target="_blank" class="button fit small">View</a></td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2 class="res-head">Cytometry Tips, Tutorials, and Protocols</h2>
        <div class="table-wrapper">
          <table class="alt">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Source</th>
                <th>Type</th>
                <th>Content</th>
                <th>Link</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>BD Biosciences: Training &amp; E-Learning</td>
                <td>Introduction to Flow Cytometry Web-Based Training</td>
                <td>Flow cytometry terms and principles. Components and functions of the fluidics, optics, and electronics systems. Cell sorting and data analysis.</td>
                <td><a href="https://www.bdbiosciences.com/us/support/s/itf_launch" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Bio-Rad: Introduction to Flow Cytometry</td>
                <td>Basics Guide</td>
                <td>Principles of the Flow Cytometer, Principles of Fluorescence, Data Analysis, Controls, Optimization, Panel Building, Troubleshooting</td>
                <td><a href="https://www.bio-rad-antibodies.com/introduction-to-flow-cytometry.html" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Boster Bio: Technical Resource Center</td>
                <td>Intro to Flow Cytometry</td>
                <td>Flow Cytometry Principles, Sample Preparation Guide, Protocols, Optimization Tips, Troubleshooting Tips, Technical Blogs</td>
                <td><a href="https://www.bosterbio.com/flow-technical-resource-center" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>CYTO University</td>
                <td>Courses and Webinars</td>
                <td>ISAC's online portal for on-demand, peer-reviewed cytometry education</td>
                <td><a href="http://www.cytou.org/store/provider/provider09.php" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Expert Cytometry</td>
                <td>Free Intro and Paid Advanced Training</td>
                <td>A Tim Bushnell-led resource with excellent education material.</td>
                <td><a href="https://expertcytometry.com/blog/" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>FlowJo University</td>
                <td>Tutorials and Training</td>
                <td>FlowJo is the industry standard for flow cytometry research. Intro and Advanced material available.</td>
                <td><a href="https://www.flowjo.com/learn/flowjo-university" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>FlowJo Webinars</td>
                <td>Webinars</td>
                <td>A library of past FlowJo webinars encompassing many topics.</td>
                <td><a href="https://flowjo.wistia.com/projects/4g79xrk22k" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Dr. Mario Roederer</td>
                <td>An informal perspective</td>
                <td>The best description of compensation on the internet.</td>
                <td><a href="http://drmr.com" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Thermo</td>
                <td>Flow Cytometry Learning Center</td>
                <td>Find courses for basic applications and techniques used in flow cytometry</td>
                <td><a href="https://www.thermofisher.com/us/en/home/life-science/cell-analysis/flow-cytometry/flow-cytometry-learning-center.html" target="_blank" class="button fit small">Visit</a></td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

